    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d44">

                <pb facs="0062" n="740" xml:id="pg740"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Dayton</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No 345.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-05-18"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 18, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> The reception of your despatch of the 27th
                    of April (No. 302) has been already acknowledged. Our information from London
                    (of a date four days later than your communication) encourages a belief that
                    more temperate views are beginning to prevail there, and a corresponding decline
                    of sensibility is observed here. I have not failed, however, to bring your
                    apprehensions of a disturbance of our relations with Great Britain to the
                    knowledge of the President, that he might take into consideration the special
                    measure of precaution which you have suggested.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">William</hi> L<hi rendition="#italic">.</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dayton</hi>, Esq., <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >&amp;c.</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
